1
00:00:01,417 --> 00:00:01,917
[调查背景] Man: Hello.

2
00:00:01,917 --> 00:00:05,514
Do you mind if I ask you some questions about your journey today?

3
00:00:05,514 --> 00:00:08,954
We're doing a customer satisfaction survey.

4
00:00:08,954 --> 00:00:12,973
Sophie: Yes.&nbsp; OK. I've got about ten minutes before my train home leaves.

5
00:00:12,973 --> 00:00:14,256
I'm on a day trip.

6
00:00:14,256 --> 00:00:15,077
Man: Great.

7
00:00:15,077 --> 00:00:15,806
Thank you.

8
00:00:15,806 --> 00:00:18,789
So first of all, could you tell me your name?

9
00:00:18,789 --> 00:00:20,775
Sophie: It's Sophie Bird. Sophie：

10
00:00:20,775 --> 00:00:22,010
Man: Thank you.

11
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:25,922
[Q1定位：what ... do = occupation n职业； Q1答案句] And would you mind telling me what you do?&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sophie: I'm a journalist.&nbsp;

12
00:00:25,922 --> 00:00:29,494
Man: Oh really? That must be interesting. Sophie: Yes. It is.

13
00:00:29,494 --> 00:00:33,394
(Q2) [定位： reason原词] Man: So was the reason for your visit here today work?

14
00:00:33,394 --> 00:00:37,460
[Q2答案句] Sophie: Actually, it's my day off.&nbsp; I came here to do some shopping.

15
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:38,460
Man: Oh right.

16
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:41,043
[Q2干扰项： 回答人先说+又说无关信息] Sophie: But I do sometimes come here for work. Sophie：

17
00:00:41,043 --> 00:00:42,277
Man: OK.

18
00:00:42,277 --> 00:00:46,337
(Q3) Now I'd like to ask some questions about your journey today, if that's OK.

19
00:00:46,337 --> 00:00:47,409
Sophie: Yes. No problem.

20
00:00:47,409 --> 00:00:51,783
[Q3定位句：station原词， back  = return] Man: Right, so can you tell me which station you're travelling back to?

21
00:00:51,783 --> 00:00:54,393
Sophie: Staunfirth, where I live. Sophie：Staunfirth，

22
00:00:54,393 --> 00:01:04,182
[Q3答案句： 拼写类 听到就要跟上， 不要等另一方确认，另一方可能有更改，但也可能只说yes] Man: Can I just check the spelling? S-T-A-U-N-F-I-R-T-H?&nbsp;

23
00:01:04,182 --> 00:01:06,034
Sophie: That's right. Sophie：

24
00:01:06,034 --> 00:01:08,330
Man: And you travelled from there this morning?

25
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:09,401
Sophie: Yes. Sophie：

26
00:01:09,401 --> 00:01:10,764
Man: OK, good.

27
00:01:10,764 --> 00:01:14,037
(Q4) Next, can I ask what kind of ticket you bought?

28
00:01:14,037 --> 00:01:17,567
I assume it wasn't a season ticket, as you don't travel every day.

29
00:01:17,567 --> 00:01:18,824
Sophie: That's right. Sophie：

30
00:01:18,824 --> 00:01:22,391
[Q4答案句] No, I just got a normal return ticket.

31
00:01:22,391 --> 00:01:26,016
(Q5) [其实还没进题] I don't have a rail card so I didn't get any discount.

32
00:01:26,016 --> 00:01:29,371
I keep meaning to get one because it's a lot cheaper.

33
00:01:29,371 --> 00:01:33,217
[Q5干扰项（不完全算干扰，因为还没进题）： 预判是数字， 听到20就写了， 但其实是20% 折扣] Man: Yes – you'd have saved 20% on your ticket today.

34
00:01:33,217 --> 00:01:38,256
[Q5定位：问的人   pay=cost，    Q5答案句：] So you paid the full price for your ticket?&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Sophie: I paid ￡23.70.&nbsp;

35
00:01:38,256 --> 00:01:39,169
Man: OK.

36
00:01:39,169 --> 00:01:41,304
Do you think that's good value for money?

37
00:01:41,304 --> 00:01:42,237
Sophie: Not really. Sophie：

38
00:01:42,237 --> 00:01:45,654
I think it's too much for a journey that only takes 45 minutes.

39
00:01:45,654 --> 00:01:48,688
Man: Yes, that's one of the main complaints we get.

40
00:01:48,688 --> 00:01:51,313
(Q6) So, you didn't buy your ticket in advance?

41
00:01:51,313 --> 00:01:52,146
Sophie: No. Sophie：

42
00:01:52,146 --> 00:01:56,708
I know it's cheaper if you buy a week in advance but I didn't know I was coming then.

43
00:01:56,708 --> 00:01:57,544
Man: I know.

44
00:01:57,544 --> 00:01:59,794
You can't always plan ahead.

45
00:01:59,794 --> 00:02:02,239
So, did you buy it this morning?

46
00:02:02,239 --> 00:02:04,325
[跟住空前上一行定位词 yesterday] Sophie: No, it was yesterday.&nbsp;

47
00:02:04,325 --> 00:02:05,296
Man: Right.

48
00:02:05,296 --> 00:02:08,724
[Q6定位句： buy=bought , at station = where(上下义)] And do you usually buy your tickets at the station?

49
00:02:08,724 --> 00:02:14,777
[Q6可能的干扰项： ticket machine， 其实是hate，所以不会是答案] Sophie: Well, I do usually but the ticket office closes early and I hate using ticket machines.&nbsp;

50
00:02:14,777 --> 00:02:18,372
I think ticket offices should be open for longer hours.

51
00:02:18,372 --> 00:02:21,634
There's always a queue for the machines and they're often out of order.

52
00:02:21,634 --> 00:02:24,567
Man: A lot of customers are saying the same thing.

53
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:29,345
[Q6答案句： 明确回答问题的信号词 to answer your question ( 属于连接词)] Sophie: So to answer your question … I got an e-ticket online.&nbsp;

54
00:02:29,345 --> 00:02:31,667
Man: OK. Thank you.

55
00:02:31,667 --> 00:02:35,465
(Q7) [跟定位词 小标题： satisfaction with journey 原词] Now I'd like to ask you about your satisfaction with your journey.

56
00:02:35,465 --> 00:02:39,374
[跟定位词空前上一行： most satisfied] So what would you say you were most satisfied with today?

57
00:02:39,374 --> 00:02:42,691
[wifi,继续跟定位] Sophie: Well, I like the wifi on the train. Sophie：

58
00:02:42,691 --> 00:02:44,571
It's improved a lot.

59
00:02:44,571 --> 00:02:47,274
It makes it easier for me to work if I want to.

60
00:02:47,274 --> 00:02:50,154
Man: That's the first time today anyone's mentioned that.

61
00:02:50,154 --> 00:02:53,318
It's good to get some positive feedback on that.

62
00:02:53,318 --> 00:02:57,235
[Q7定位：问句 同替： not safisfied= least +adj 表示否定。 强调weren't 发音] Man: And, is there anything you weren't satisfied with?

63
00:02:57,235 --> 00:03:08,242
[Q7答案句：delay。   but.后面跟重点信息， this morning = today 扩展记忆区间] Sophie: Well, normally, the trains run on time and are pretty reliable but today there was a delay; the train was about 15 minutes behind schedule. Sophie：

64
00:03:08,242 --> 00:03:10,352
Man: OK. I'll put that down.

65
00:03:10,352 --> 00:03:15,072
(Q8) [Q8跟定位： 小标题原词] Now I'd also like to ask about the facilities at this station.

66
00:03:15,072 --> 00:03:18,676
You've probably noticed that the whole station's been upgraded.

67
00:03:18,676 --> 00:03:21,510
[Q8定位词： most satisfied] What are you most satisfied with?

68
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:30,025
[the amount of = how much， 表示「数量」 ，听 是什么东西的数量，      give = provide 被动语态+扩展记忆区间] Sophie: I think the best thing is that they've improved the amount of information about train times etc. that's given to passengers.&nbsp;

69
00:03:30,025 --> 00:03:37,394
– it's much clearer – before there was only one board and I couldn't always see it properly – which was frustrating. ——

70
00:03:37,394 --> 00:03:38,442
Man: That's good.

71
00:03:38,442 --> 00:03:41,316
(Q9) [Q9定位： not satisfied=least 同Q7] And is there anything you're not satisfied with?

72
00:03:41,316 --> 00:03:43,016
Sophie: Let's see … Sophie：

73
00:03:43,016 --> 00:03:46,428
I think things have generally improved a lot.

74
00:03:46,428 --> 00:03:51,040
The trains are much more modern and I like the new café.

75
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:56,662
[Q9答案句： not enough = lack of 缺少…，   especially=particularly 后面跟出答案] But one thing is that there aren't enough places to sit down, especially on the platforms.

76
00:03:56,662 --> 00:04:02,411
Man: OK – so I'll put 'seating' down, shall I, as the thing you're least satisfied with?

77
00:04:02,411 --> 00:04:04,175
Sophie: Yes. Sophie：

78
00:04:04,175 --> 00:04:07,745
(Q10) Man: Can I ask your opinion about some of the other facilities?

79
00:04:07,745 --> 00:04:15,275
[🟢Q10定位词：Neither……nor 原词] We'd like feedback on whether people are satisfied, dissatisfied or neither satisfied nor dissatisfied.

80
00:04:15,275 --> 00:04:16,107
Sophie: OK. Sophie：

81
00:04:16,107 --> 00:04:19,807
[Q10答案句： 听到了预测时的一类东西 就要先写上] Man: What about the parking at the station?

82
00:04:19,807 --> 00:04:24,065
Sophie: Well to be honest, I don't really have an opinion as I never use it.&nbsp;

83
00:04:24,065 --> 00:04:27,559
Man: So, neither satisfied nor dissatisfied for that then.

84
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:30,249
[Q10通过另一方回答，辅助确认答案] Sophie: Yes, I suppose so …&nbsp;

85
00:04:30,249 --> 00:04:32,749
Man: OK, and what about …?

